        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "064a8930-9ad9-59e9-ac7c-c9b585b1040b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James B. Donovan, Francis Gary Powers, Rudolf Abel, Vilyam \"Willie\" Genrikhovich Fisher, Scott Shepherd\n- Works: Bridge of Spies, Side Effects, Jason Bourne\n- Topics: Cold War, U-2 incident, Soviet intelligence\n\nFacts:\n- Rudolf Abel, whose real name was Vilyam \"Willie\" Genrikhovich Fisher, was born on July 11, 1903, and was a Soviet intelligence officer.\n- In 1960, Francis Gary Powers was a U.S. Air Force pilot whose U-2 spy plane was shot down over the Soviet Union.\n- Bridge of Spies is set during the Cold War and tells the story of lawyer James B. Donovan negotiating the release of Francis Gary Powers in exchange for Rudolf Abel.\n- In Bridge of Spies, James B. Donovan represents Rudolf Abel at trial while Abel is a convicted Soviet KGB spy in United States custody.\n- Rudolf Abel died on November 15, 1971.\n- Scott Shepherd is an American film, theater, and television actor known for appearing in Bridge of Spies, Side Effects, and Jason Bourne.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f5f0c67d-9422-5605-94c2-ad9152106144",
        "text": "Page: Bridge of Spies (film). Sentence: Set during the Cold War, the film tells the story of lawyer James B. Donovan, who is entrusted with negotiating the release of Francis Gary Powers—a U.S. Air Force pilot whose U-2 spy plane was shot down over the Soviet Union in 1960—in exchange for Rudolf Abel, a convicted Soviet KGB spy held under the custody of the United States, whom he represented at trial.\nPage: Rudolf Abel. Sentence: Rudolf Ivanovich Abel (Russian: Рудольф Иванович Абель ), real name Vilyam \"Willie\" Genrikhovich Fisher (Вильям \"Вилли\" Генрихович Фишер), (July 11, 1903 – November 15, 1971) was a Soviet intelligence officer.\nPage: Scott Shepherd (actor). Sentence: Scott Shepherd is an American film, theater, and television actor, best known for his appearances in the films \"Bridge of Spies\", \"Side Effects\" and \"Jason Bourne\".",
